  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Connect all given points in the plane with straight edges. The cost of joining <code>[x1,y1]</code> to <code>[x2,y2]</code> is <code>|x1-x2| + |y1-y2|</code>. Return the smallest possible sum of costs such that every point can reach every other point through the selected edges.</p>\n  <p>You may choose an edge between any two points. Cycles cannot reduce the minimum cost, so consider how to build a minimum spanning tree of this implicit complete graph.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> points = [[0,0],[2,2],[3,10],[5,2],[7,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 20\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Edges with costs 4, 3, 9 and 4 connect all five points for 20.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> points = [[1,1],[2,2],[3,3]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Joining consecutive diagonal neighbors costs 2 each.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> points = [[0,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> One point needs no edges.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= points.length &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n    <li>Each point is a distinct pair of integers <code>[x,y]</code> with <code>-1000 &lt;= x,y &lt;= 1000</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
